What is Peripheral Vascular Devices?
Peripheral vascular devices encompass a broad portfolio of catheter‑based systems and implantable solutions that enable clinicians to perform percutaneous interventions across the peripheral circulatory network. From balloon angioplasty that dilates narrowed arterial segments to drug‑eluting stents that inhibit restenosis, these technologies empower physicians to treat complex atherosclerotic lesions with reduced procedural trauma. Emerging platforms such as bio‑resorbable scaffolds, laser atherectomy, and IoT‑enabled guidewires further expand therapeutic options, aligning with value‑based care models that prioritize rapid recovery and lower overall cost of care.
