Key Market Drivers
1. Demographic Shifts and Disease Prevalence
The aging global population-projected to reach one in six people over 60 by 2030 (World Health Organization)-and the escalating burden of diabetes (over 537 million adults in 2021, expected 783 million by 2045, International Diabetes Federation) create a sizable patient pool for peripheral vascular interventions. PAD prevalence rises to more than 12 % among those aged 65+, fueling demand for endovascular solutions.
2. Technological Innovation
Breakthroughs in drug‑eluting stents, bio‑resorbable scaffolds, atherectomy platforms, and imaging‑guided navigation have markedly improved clinical outcomes, encouraging physicians to replace surgical bypass with percutaneous therapies. Integration of digital sensors and remote monitoring further enhances procedural precision and post‑procedure management.
